# Validation with Zod

## Location & naming

All schemas in `src/lib/validators/{domain}.ts`.

```typescript
export const createBeatSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(100),
  genre: z.string().min(1),
  bpm: z.number().int().min(40).max(300).optional(),
});

export type CreateBeatInput = z.infer<typeof createBeatSchema>;
```

- Schema: `{action}{Domain}Schema` — `createBeatSchema`, `beatFilterSchema`
- Type: `{Action}{Domain}Input` — `CreateBeatInput`, `BeatFilterInput`

## Usage

- Parse in API routes before services: `const input = schema.parse(body)`.
- Use `z.coerce` for query params that arrive as strings.
- Compose schemas with `.merge()` or `.extend()`.
- Use `formatZodError()` from `@/lib/errors` for user-friendly messages.
